    "name": "jc3248w535",
    "title": "Guition JC3248W535",
    "maker": "guition",
    "part": "JC3248W535",
    "revision": "V1.0",
    "description": "3.5-inch 320x480 AXS15231B on QSPI, its touch in the same chip on I2C; an ESP32-S3 with 16 MB flash and 8 MB octal PSRAM",
    "notes": [
        "The display and the touch are one chip, the AXS15231B: the display on QSPI through DGX, the touch on I2C at 0x3B through espressif/esp_lcd_axs15231b.",
        "The touch reads one finger, where the AXS15231B tells two: the driver of Espressif, espressif/esp_lcd_axs15231b 2.1.1~1, gives every point the place of the first (touch_axs15231b_read_data).",
        "The schematic names the lines of the touch twice and differently: the block of the pull-ups R3, R4 has TP_SCL on IO4 and TP_SDA on IO8, the connector of the panel has TP-SDA on IO4 and TP-SCL on IO8. The board answers with SDA on 4 and SCL on 8.",
        "The reset of the panel is the reset line of the chip (EN), not a GPIO.",
        "The amplifier has no enable line: its CTRL is held up through R23, 1 MOhm, so it is on whenever there is power. It has no volume of its own: a program scales its samples.",
        "GPIO5 is the battery divider (33k over 100k, through R25) and contact 1 of P2 at once."
    ],
